Classification Justification

SO-F-003 defines the interpretation capability required to transform relevant observations into an operationally meaningful context.

It is derived from the root Functional Objective SO-F-001 and operates downstream of the perception capability established by SO-F-002.

Its responsibility is limited to interpretation and contextual understanding. Decision generation and action execution remain outside its scope.

---

Classification Notes

- Derived directly from SO-F-001.
- Operationally follows SO-F-002.
- Establishes the interpretation stage of the adaptive processing pipeline.
- Serves as an upstream capability for future decision-generation objectives.
- May become the parent of future context-interpretation objectives as the architecture is further decomposed.
